{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1296 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "098cc6684b2c7d8a44428164c18ab80caa34da33f360c080fe9db3a289ef5f6e" :edb/db-before-t 1295 :edb/db-after-t 1296 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534608 50 #inst "2026-10-08T02:19:54.808Z" 13194139534608 true] [17592186064138 1020 #edb/ref 17592186298548 13194139534608 true] [17592186064138 1020 #edb/ref 17592186298552 13194139534608 true] [17592186064139 1020 #edb/ref 17592186298555 13194139534608 true] [17592186064139 1020 #edb/ref 17592186298562 13194139534608 true] [17592186064774 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534608 true] [17592186064774 1100 "$\\int \\frac{{cos}^{3}⁡x+{cot}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" 13194139534608 true] [17592186064774 1100 "What is $\\displaystyle \\int\\frac{\\cos^{3} x + \\cot^{2} x}{\\cos^{2} x}dx$?" 13194139534608 false] [17592186064774 1145 "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{{cos}^{3}⁡x+{cot}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}({cos}^{3}⁡x+{cot}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe then use the fact that ${cot}^{2}⁡x=\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}$ to express this as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}({cos}^{3}⁡x+\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x})\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{cos}^{3}⁡x+{cot}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}({cos}^{3}⁡x+\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot {cos}^{3}⁡x+\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+{csc}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534608 true] [17592186298548 1017 #edb/ref 17592186298549 13194139534608 true] [17592186298548 1089 "q-352858" 13194139534608 true] [17592186298548 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534608 true] [17592186298548 1100 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /8}\\frac{\\operatorname{cot}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534608 true] [17592186298548 1113 #uuid "afef5694-bf50-563b-a88c-5f1ccf492bde" 13194139534608 true] [17592186298548 1145 "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /8}\\frac{\\operatorname{cot}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /8}\\operatorname{cot}⁡4x\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThen, we use the fact that $\\operatorname{cot}⁡4x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}$ and $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡4x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /8}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /8}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=4x.$ Then $\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u.$ \n\nNow, we fill the table for the limits of integration, according to the rule $u=4x.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{8}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ |\n\nTherefore, the integral in terms of the new variable is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /8}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u{|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(sin\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-sin\\,(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534608 true] [17592186298549 1000 #edb/ref 17592186298550 13194139534608 true] [17592186298549 1000 #edb/ref 17592186298551 13194139534608 true] [17592186298549 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534608 true] [17592186298549 1041 "field-1" 13194139534608 true] [17592186298549 1104 #edb/ref 17592186298551 13194139534608 true] [17592186298549 1110 #uuid "f0248f05-f4bb-5916-9e44-4dee6f81dc37" 13194139534608 true] [17592186298550 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139534608 true] [17592186298550 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534608 true] [17592186298550 1111 #uuid "3e614d8e-5811-579d-b04a-473c177e6097" 13194139534608 true] [17592186298551 1034 "\\frac{1}{4}" 13194139534608 true] [17592186298551 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534608 true] [17592186298551 1111 #uuid "88a920aa-976c-5392-ab89-a8afb89dfead" 13194139534608 true] [17592186298552 1017 #edb/ref 17592186298553 13194139534608 true] [17592186298552 1089 "q-352868" 13194139534608 true] [17592186298552 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534608 true] [17592186298552 1100 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534608 true] [17592186298552 1113 #uuid "d5555438-060c-5bd3-a19d-6d830dc51bce" 13194139534608 true] [17592186298552 1145 "We can rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThen, we use the fact that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}$ and $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡4x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=4x.$ Then $\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u.$\n\nNow, we fill the table for the limits of integration, according to the rule $u=4x.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{12}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ |\n\nTherefore, the integral in terms of the new variable is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u{|}_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}(cos\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{3})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}(\\frac{1}{2}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534608 true] [17592186298553 1000 #edb/ref 17592186298554 13194139534608 true] [17592186298553 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534608 true] [17592186298553 1041 "field-1" 13194139534608 true] [17592186298553 1104 #edb/ref 17592186298554 13194139534608 true] [17592186298553 1110 #uuid "12018ba6-d93d-59f7-9f7e-13760e380cde" 13194139534608 true] [17592186298554 1034 "\\frac{1}{8}" 13194139534608 true] [17592186298554 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534608 true] [17592186298554 1111 #uuid "ff66d701-ccee-551c-96f2-ca7da2e776d9" 13194139534608 true] [17592186298555 1017 #edb/ref 17592186298556 13194139534608 true] [17592186298555 1089 "q-49256" 13194139534608 true] [17592186298555 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534608 true] [17592186298555 1100 "Calculate $\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡3x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" 13194139534608 true] [17592186298555 1113 #uuid "fc5d1374-23d8-5057-a23d-f12014c4a689" 13194139534608 true] [17592186298555 1145 "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡3x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡3x\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe then use the fact that $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x}=\\operatorname{sec}⁡3x$ to express this as\n\n$$\n\\int {sec}^{2}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=3x.$ Then $\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int {sec}^{2}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡u\\cdot \\,\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int {sec}^{2}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡3x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534608 true] [17592186298556 1000 #edb/ref 17592186298557 13194139534608 true] [17592186298556 1000 #edb/ref 17592186298558 13194139534608 true] [17592186298556 1000 #edb/ref 17592186298559 13194139534608 true] [17592186298556 1000 #edb/ref 17592186298560 13194139534608 true] [17592186298556 1000 #edb/ref 17592186298561 13194139534608 true] [17592186298556 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534608 true] [17592186298556 1041 "selection" 13194139534608 true] [17592186298556 1104 #edb/ref 17592186298557 13194139534608 true] [17592186298556 1110 #uuid "0a6cac14-08de-54a8-8903-80c7cc92480a" 13194139534608 true] [17592186298557 1034 "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡3x+C" 13194139534608 true] [17592186298557 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534608 true] [17592186298557 1111 #uuid "a8c3027e-65bf-5167-9725-2ee745184d93" 13194139534608 true] [17592186298558 1034 "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C" 13194139534608 true] [17592186298558 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534608 true] [17592186298558 1111 #uuid "3191b9f4-02cf-5cd6-8864-c940680d0a30" 13194139534608 true] [17592186298559 1034 "\\frac{1}{3}{sec}^{2}⁡3x+C" 13194139534608 true] [17592186298559 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534608 true] [17592186298559 1111 #uuid "81564b7e-7f70-5f3f-90b4-fefee4ac29cb" 13194139534608 true] [17592186298560 1034 "\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})+C" 13194139534608 true] [17592186298560 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534608 true] [17592186298560 1111 #uuid "51029c53-8df7-5703-8d0b-3beba0a8d5d6" 13194139534608 true] [17592186298561 1034 "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C" 13194139534608 true] [17592186298561 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534608 true] [17592186298561 1111 #uuid "00f92431-15b5-5ad4-8554-3d0397c3f125" 13194139534608 true] [17592186298562 10